  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Given the vector $u$ has magnitude $4$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $9,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${75}^{\u2218}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n$ and round your final answer to **one decimal place** where appropriate.\n\n$u\\times v\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =4\\cdot 9\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{75}^{\u2218}\\cdot n \\\\  & =36\\cdot (0.965\\,92\u2026)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(34.773\\,32\u2026)\\cdot n \\\\  & \u224834.8n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
